  combinedLines: Cold winds howl through the shattered ruins of the castle. Above,
    a relentless rain of blood stains the sky. The city is a graveyard. Mothers freeze
    in death, clutching starved infants. | others lie crushed under fallen stone,
    or collapsed from sheer exhaustion. | Yet, amid the pitch-black night, a thirteen-year-old
    girl kneels in the dirt. With trembling hands, she gathers the ash and remains
    of the dead, lighting a final, defiant pyre.
